<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The Center's REAL entry point.

     The backend menuitem (views/channel_center_views.xml) hangs under
     "CRM Center → Care Command Setup", which is correct — and, on vietuat,
     unreachable: users land in the /bizapp CMS shell, whose app switcher
     offers only its own apps, and /odoo redirects straight back into it. That
     is the ledger §5.41 sibling trap (the telemonitoring/twin menus have the
     same problem), and it was found by driving the real login in CC-C browser
     QA: the Center could only be opened by deep link.

     So the Center also seeds a CMS sidebar item, directly after Care Command
     in the same CRM section — connecting a channel belongs next to working the
     conversations it produces.

     A SIBLING, deliberately not a child: cms_sidebar.js:124 treats "items with
     children as expandable groups; leaves navigate", so parenting this under
     Care Command would have turned Care Command itself into a non-navigating
     accordion — a regression on the existing entry. Caught by driving the real
     sidebar, not by reading the model.

     NO noupdate: the item stays updatable on upgrade (ledger
     noupdate-seed-cutover). Ungated (no role_ids) like the sibling Care
     Command item — `center_overview` group-gates the data server-side and the
     component renders that refusal as an honest inline message rather than an
     error dialog. -->
<odoo>

    <record id="item_channel_center" model="cms.sidebar.item">
        <field name="name">Channel Center</field>
        <field name="section_id" ref="health_cms_sidebar.section_crm"/>
        <!-- Explicitly FALSE, not merely absent: an XML data update only
             writes the fields it names, so dropping `parent_id` from this
             record would have left an earlier value in place (it did — the
             item stayed a hidden child of Care Command through one deploy). -->
        <field name="parent_id" eval="False"/>
        <field name="sequence">12</field>
        <field name="icon">fa fa-plug</field>
        <field name="action_xmlid">health_care_command_channels.action_channel_center</field>
        <field name="action_tag">channel_center</field>
        <field name="match_action_tags">channel_center</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
